>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `remove_arith`, `remove_arith_split`

``` hol4
linarithData.remove_arith : string -> unit
linarithData.remove_arith_split : string -> unit
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Remove persistent linarith facts or operator-splitting rules.

Each function records and immediately applies a persistent `REMOVE` delta
for its corresponding theorem set. The removal is inherited by child
theories and remains effective when declarations are reloaded. Names may
use database form `Theory.name`; kernel form `Theory$name` is also
recognised, and an unqualified `name` is resolved against the theory the
call is made in. That resolution happens where the call is written, so
the recorded delta designates the same declaration in every descendant
theory that replays it. Removing an absent, valid name is harmless. The
`[arith]` and `[arith_split]` sets are independent.

Both sets hold user declarations only. The operator-splitting rules a
linarith instance supplies through its `pre_split` field are built in,
do not belong to the `[arith_split]` set, and cannot be removed.

### Failure

Fails if a supplied `Theory.name` database name cannot be parsed, in
particular if it carries more than one dot. A string in `Theory$name`
kernel form is used directly as a table key. Removing an absent name does
not fail.

### Example

The following declarations are removed from their separate sets in the
current theory.

``` hol4
Theorem temporary_arith_fact[arith]:
  (0 : num) <= 1
Proof
  simp []
QED

Theorem temporary_arith_split[arith_split]:
  !P b x y.
    P (if b then (x : num) else y) <=>
    (b ==> P x) /\ (~b ==> P y)
Proof
  rw []
QED

val linarith_doc_theory = Theory.current_theory ();

val _ =
  linarithData.remove_arith
    (linarith_doc_theory ^ ".temporary_arith_fact");

val _ =
  linarithData.remove_arith_split
    (linarith_doc_theory ^ ".temporary_arith_split");
```

